## How recursive CTEs work

Recursive CTEs allow a query to repeatedly join a table to itself until it reaches a termination condition. In this hierarchy query:

- The anchor member selects top-level categories with `parent_id IS NULL`.
- The recursive member joins each child category back to the CTE on `parent_id = id`.
- Each recursion level appends the child name to the path and increments depth.
- The recursion stops automatically when no more child rows match.

This approach is efficient for adjacency-list hierarchies because it avoids multiple separate queries and produces a full tree traversal in a single statement.
